          "write": "+ on ortho and para"
        },
        {
          "say": "Step three: a base removes H plus and the aromatic ring comes back.",
          "write": "3. −H⁺, ring restored"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The main reactions",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Nitration: concentrated nitric and sulfuric acids make the nitronium ion.",
          "write": "NO₂⁺ (conc. HNO₃/H₂SO₄)"
        },
        {
          "say": "Halogenation needs a Lewis acid, like iron tribromide, to polarise bromine.",
          "write": "Br₂ / FeBr₃ → C₆H₅Br"
        },
        {
          "say": "Friedel–Crafts alkylation can rearrange, and adds more than once.",
          "write": "alkylation: rearranges"
        },
        {
          "say": "1-chloropropane gives mostly isopropylbenzene, not propylbenzene.",
          "write": "✗ propylbenzene"
        },
        {
          "say": "Acylation is safe. The acylium ion doesn't rearrange and stops after one.",
          "write": "RCOCl / AlCl₃ → ketone"
        },
        {
          "say": "Acylate, then reduce the ketone, to get a straight chain.",
          "write": "acylate → reduce"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Where does the next group go?",
